-- title:
--   The degree-n unramified extension ℚₚ(μ_{pⁿ-1})
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $n$ a positive natural number, and inside the algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl p` of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ (carrying the norm extending the $p$-adic absolute value) let $K$ be the intermediate field $\mathbb{Q}_p$-generated by the set $\{\zeta : \zeta^{p^n-1} = 1\}$ of all $(p^n-1)$-st roots of unity, the exponent being formed with truncated subtraction. The assertion is the conjunction of four statements: (i) $K$ is Galois over $\mathbb{Q}_p$, in the sense of Mathlib's `IsGalois`; (ii) the $\mathbb{Q}_p$-dimension of $K$ equals $n$; (iii) every non-zero $x \in K$ has $\|x\| = p^k$ for some integer $k$, so that the value group of $K$ is already that of $\mathbb{Q}_p$, i.e. $K/\mathbb{Q}_p$ is unramified; and (iv) every $x \in K$ of norm $1$ is approximated by a root of unity: there is $\zeta \in$ `PadicAlgCl p` with $\zeta^{p^n-1} = 1$ and $\|x - \zeta\| < 1$, the Teichmüller lifting of the residue field $\mathbb{F}_{p^n}$.
--
--   This is the structure theorem for the unramified extension of $\mathbb{Q}_p$ of degree $n$, realised concretely as $\mathbb{Q}_p(\mu_{p^n-1})$ inside a fixed algebraic closure, together with its value group and Teichmüller representatives; it specialises to the base field $\mathbb{Q}_p$ the general results on adjoining $(q^N-1)$-st roots of unity to a finite extension $K$ of $\mathbb{Q}_q$, namely that the relative degree is the order of $\#\kappa$ in $\mathbb{Z}/(q^N-1)$, that no new norms arise, and that the extension is finite and normal. It is used in the local analysis of inertia subgroups and of norms of $p^n-1$ powers in cyclotomic towers, and thence in the place-decomposition cocycle computations.
-- source:
